Z||000011||maryjane||11-07-2001||10:29 PM||||Depends--If you buy right after a split, price is low. A good growth company stock can recoup its worth in 18 mos. Splits again. You now have twice as much stock. Price per share is same (approx) as when you bought the original amt, but overall value is doubled.(twice as many shares) The money you spend on filling your tank is real, the value you hold in stock is only on paper unless you sell. If you spend $100 per month on gas, that is  $300/qtr. At the current declared Exxon dividend of 23cents/share, you would have to own 1343 shares to break even just off of your quarterly dividend. Course, if you were to buy that many shares outright, at todays price/per share, it would cost you over $49,000 .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
